  "2015 P2 Q1": {"marks":9,"subject":"An altitude, a median, and where they meet.","rows":[{"for":"calculate gradient of AB","shows":"\\(m_{\\text{AB}} = -3\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"use property of perpendicular lines","shows":"\\(m_{\\text{alt}} = \\dfrac{1}{3}\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"substitute into general equation of a line","shows":"\\(y - 3 = \\dfrac{1}{3}(x - 13)\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"demonstrate result","shows":"\\(\\ldots \\Rightarrow x - 3y = 4\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"calculate midpoint of AC","shows":"\\(\\text{M}_{\\text{AC}} = (4, 5)\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"calculate gradient of median","shows":"\\(m_{\\text{BM}} = 2\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"determine equation of median","shows":"\\(y = 2x - 3\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"calculate \\(x\\) or \\(y\\) coordinate","shows":"\\(x = 1\\) or \\(y = -1\\)","part":"(c)"},{"for":"calculate remaining coordinate of the point of intersection","shows":"\\(y = -1\\) or \\(x = 1\\)","part":"(c)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. •³ is only available as a consequence of trying to find and use a perpendicular gradient.","(a) 2. •⁴ is only available if there is/are appropriate intermediate lines of working between •³ and •⁴.","(a) 3. The ONLY acceptable variations for the final equation for the line in •⁴ are \\(4 = x - 3y\\), \\(-3y + x = 4\\), \\(4 = -3y + x\\).","(b) 4. •⁶ and •⁷ are not available to candidates who do not use a midpoint.","(b) 5. •⁷ is only available as a consequence of using a non-perpendicular gradient and a midpoint.","(b) 6. Candidates who find either the median through A or the median through C or a side of the triangle gain 1 mark out of 3.","(b) 7. At •⁷ accept \\(y - (-5) = 2(x - (-1))\\), \\(y - 5 = 2(x - 4)\\), \\(y - 2x + 3 = 0\\) or any other rearrangement of the equation.","(c) 8. If the candidate's 'median' is either a vertical or horizontal line then award 1 out of 2 if both coordinates are correct, otherwise award 0."]},
